            <ArticleTitle>Cardiac tamponade in a patient with severe dengue fever.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>701-705</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0037-86822017000500701</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1590/0037-8682-0361-2016</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 26-year-old postpartum female presented with symptoms characteristic of dengue fever on the 16th day of puerperium. On the third day of the illness, the patient presented a clinical picture consistent with shock. Tests determined primary infection with dengue virus serotype 2. Cardiac tamponade was confirmed by echocardiography. This rare manifestation is described in a patient without any associated comorbidity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
